Package: pollmap
Title: Spatial Modelling of Pollination Supply, Demand and Species Distributions
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", 
           email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com", 
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(affiliation = "Gyeongkuk National University"))
Description: A unified, raster-native framework for mapping wild-bee
    pollination in agricultural landscapes. It implements the distance-decay
    family of land-use models (Lonsdorf and colleagues 2009
    <doi:10.1093/aob/mcp069>; the seasonal, guild-based formulation used in
    InVEST following Kennedy and colleagues 2013
    <doi:10.1111/ele.12082>; and the quality-weighted, edge-sensitive
    variant of Rahimi and colleagues 2021 <doi:10.1186/s41610-021-00189-8>),
    couples species-distribution models to pollination-service maps, and links
    pollination supply to crop pollinator-dependence demand. The package is
    designed for reproducible, transparent ecological analysis rather than
    economic valuation.
